A note before the per-item summary: gpt-6-sol's parallel pass was landing edits in the same working tree while I worked. My whole-file rewrite of the spec was rejected for that reason, so I switched to targeted edits on top of the current text rather than overwriting the other pass. Where the other pass had already addressed a finding, I kept its text and only tightened what was inconsistent or under-specified.

## Item 1: gate decision reads (P1)

The other pass had already specified initial cursor minting at wrap, the per-outcome transitions, the two-read bound on gap, and serialization by the composition (`docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:120-147`). I added what was still open:

- `docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:109-116`: what a decision value may be, including an immutable query value, and that `verify` is then a query over it with the request as bindings, the shape `dao.space.query/q` has (verified against `src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:1599-1606`).
- `docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:135-139`: what `verify` receives once the gate is ended, the `{:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}` marker, so "becomes ended" has a defined effect.
- `docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:79-86`: the four prohibitions now name the decision read as "a bounded read on a composed decision medium" rather than a fixed count, matching the gate text.

## Item 2: ShiBi fit (P1)

Chose path (b) and marked (a) a non-goal, in all three places:

- `docs/design/dao.shibi.md:20-44`: the two-interpreter fit stated as the one chosen path: the index interpreter publishes the tuple space's current query value as the decision; the query interpreter is `verify`, the required adapter contract, a Datalog query over that value with the request as bindings.
- `docs/design/dao.shibi.md:46-56`: limits stated precisely: one snapshot per call, cost bounded by the composition, no opening or waiting inside `verify`, staleness bounded by index cadence and medium eviction, fail-closed on the `none` and `ended` markers, a decision is not a fact unless emitted.
- `docs/design/dao.shibi.md:58-63`: request-specific decisions awaited over streams declared a non-goal for this version, with the reason (a gate awaiting an answer would wait).
- `docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:583-589`: section 7 names the same chosen path and points at the ShiBi doc for the contract and its limits.

