## Item 5: pair gap to loss (P2)

The other pass's sentence said the link "applies its existing resend rule to outstanding reads" after the gap, which contradicts the channel-loss path it invokes. Fixed:

- `docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:401-410`: an `in` gap closes the channel reader for the link; the link observes `end`, abandons outstanding ids (not re-sent), reports each abandoned `append!` as `append-unknown`, and reattachment on the same pair descriptor mints a fresh `in` cursor at `:newest`; the gap is never surfaced as a source's gap.
- `docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:267-269`: the channel-loss rule now names the pair adapter's gap-or-end closure as one of its three causes.
- `docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:149-151`: slice 7 proves the rule.

